  "scoreRationale": {
    "shapeVolume": "Puffed connected toque lobes and curved band, softer hair/moustache and head edges, rebuilt cuffs/collar/apron and a coherent back bow visibly improve the source. Target fabric folds are longer and more fluid; the compact native version remains convincing and readable within the fixed envelope.",
    "color": "Omar retains amber/tan skin, blue-black fringe/moustache, ivory toque/coat, teal apron/tie and dark footwear. It remains clearly distinct from the separate family concept palette.",
    "lightingHighlights": "Creamy whites retain volume instead of source white clipping, and broad symmetric illumination separates dark hair lobes without a strong lateral light or ground shadow. Highlights are quieter than the target.",
    "materialDetail": "Collar, cuff rolls, apron straps and pocket rim, tie tails and back knot read as purposeful layered geometry at logical size. The finish is restrained and less ornate than target stitching.",
    "artifactFreeReadability": "No material tears, seams, flicker, collapsed limbs/garments, alpha debris, clipping or black dead spots were found in the288-frame sheets and sampled actual playback. Skin, ivory, teal and navy masses remain legible on light, gray and dark backgrounds."
  },
  "observations": [
    {
      "area": "identity and shape",
      "evidence": "The original front S and rear N conventions remain visibly correct. The stepped white source toque is replaced by a rounded puff crown over a curved band, and the original amber face, cropped dark fringe and paired moustache remain recognizable."
    },
    {
      "area": "garment construction",
      "evidence": "The ivory collar and rolled cuffs separate from skin and torso; teal shoulder straps, bib/pocket rim and waist details give the front structure. The back knot and tails complete the design rather than leaving an unexplained flat apron slab. Serving and work poses retain connected sleeves and intact hands."
    },
    {
      "area": "color and light",
      "evidence": "The common warm soft treatment preserves distinct cream, teal, amber and navy values in every facing. Back hair retains broad form separation, and hat shading has no source-like overexposed rectangular dead zone. Three-background and repeated logical-size previews remain clean."
    },
    {
      "area": "animation and food overlays",
      "evidence": "All catalog and supplemental frame sequences were inspected. Small native head/body tilts remain coherent without topology pops or garment collapse. Salmon and cucumber remain the original separately identified2D food cutouts, with original camera-facing behavior and source-relative hand/attachment placement. No new occlusion defect was found."
    },
    {
      "area": "technical result",
      "evidence": "Fresh Blender reopening and evaluation of original/candidate catalog and runtime projects confirms exact rest bones, action signatures, source root/bone/attachment matrices and visibility, stable evaluated topology and exact packed food bytes. Palm centroid numerical differences remain below5e-7world units."
    }
  ],
  "blockers": [],
  "remainingDifferences": [
    "Native toque uses compact rounded puff volumes rather than the target's long gathered folds; side crown transitions retain mild broad faceting. It still provides the required soft dimensional improvement over the original within the locked height and registration.",
    "Target features a broader displayed apron pocket, larger exposed shoes, larger eyes and more micro-stitching. These are optional design details; the native result keeps the fixed functional proportions/contacts and adds enough legible garment construction without matching the target's enlarged presentation.",
    "The native light is calmer and less glossy/rimmed than ImageGen, preserving horizontal symmetry and avoiding the target's bright edge halo.",
    "The existing camera-facing food cutouts can read as overlays near the chin and reveal a plate sliver in rear cucumber views. This behavior and exact geometry/UV/depth drivers match the original sources and were preserved as required."
  ],
